Early on I suggest picking among your existing weapons
using base damage, weight and single handed wield as
considerations.  You might want to wield a unicorn horn or
elven broadsword until you have an artifact good enough to
ascend with.

I think Stormbringer is your best option.  If you don't have
a +FoD in your open inventory at the time you get crowned,
you get that book.  If you manage to have a +FoD in your
open inventory at the time you are crowned, you get
Stormbringer.  I suggest that you now have a goal of getting
that spellbook then getting crowned once you have it.

> I haven't received any wishes yet.

That's not much correlated with how many artifacts exist
in the game - Wishing for an artifact has chances of failure
based on the number of existing artifacts.  Note that even
though Magicbane has evaporated it "exists" in this game.
"Exists" means "have been created in this game" for this
purpose.  Below I suggest getting Stromy without wishing
for an artifact -

I'd do the Castle, wish for a blessed +FoD as your second
wish, read it, then go get crowned.  Then exericse Stormy
on popcorn monsters until you get offered to enhnace it,
enhance it, then resume exploring below the Castle.

But if you manage to get one of the other powerful artifact
weapons, use it as your primary wield and don't bother with
Stormy.

> I think I've used all my skill slots. (My dagger is at
> expert, attack spells at expert, and divination at expert)
> ... I'm at experience level 19.

If you are at XP=19 then you have not used all of your
skill slots.  You get one slot per level and the maximum
level is XP=30 giving 29 skill slots.  A wizard can max
out dagger plus *all* spell schools and have 4 slots left.
That's good enough to enhance one major artifact weapon
to Basic and still have 3 left for something fun like pole
arm (spetum from a troll) to Skilled for the castles or 3
other artifact classes to Basic for style.  Anyways, skill
slots are not a limited resource for wizards.

> Should I just get Sting or something?

If you ever plan on using a sacrifest for artifacts, the
number of existing artifacts (MB "exists" in this game)
effects the chances.  So if you'll ever do a sacrifice loop,
do it before naming either Sting or Orcrist.

Until getting a good artifact weapon it doesn't hurt to wield
Sting but compare base damage against non-artifact
weapons.  Sting competes with other weapons for
damage compared to MB that gets added reasons.

